{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update-stage9.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn spent on the one open lead: whether an InstallSnapshot that is current in term but older in index can rewind a receiver's applied state. Instead of more reading I built the probe its discriminator called for and requested the fixed execution (valid:true).\\n\\nProbe (draft/assurance_install_rewind.go): three rounds of 25 warm commands, isolate one follower, 60 further commands through the remaining quorum so the leader compacts past that follower's next index, reconnect, then 1.2s of polling every 2ms across all three nodes. It records each node's applied index, snapshot index and log store last index, tracks the maximum applied index seen, any applied-index decrease with the snapshot index and log store last index at that moment, snapshot-index changes, and how many poll ticks showed the snapshot index above the log store last index (the install signature). Per node it emits recovered_node_probe_end when that signature was seen and steady_node_probe_end otherwise, with all operands (prior/new applied index, decrease_count, indices at the decrease) so a negative or positive result is inspectable.\\n\\nExperiment request: requirement stated as a protection (no delivered InstallSnapshot in this scenario moves a receiver's applied index backwards; a request whose snapshot index is below the receiver's applied state would appear as an applied-index decrease), responsibility at receiver-side admission and applied-state bookkeeping, anchors at Raft.installSnapshot (raft.go:1814-1950), Raft.processLogs (raft.go:1292-1358) and raftState.getLastIndex (state.go:159-163). Two comparisons, role-specific event names to avoid the correlation defect from the earlier successor: the recovered node (applicability install_signature_seen true) and the steady nodes in the same execution (install_signature_seen false), both asserting observed_applied_decrease false.\\n\\nNative local feedback, flagged in the investigation limitations as not retained evidence: the probe reached the install state (recovered node snapshot index 257 above log store last index 197 for 1234 poll ticks) with applied state monotone (max 257, decrease_count 0) while the other two nodes reported no install signature — so locally the concern was not reproduced in this scenario. The investigation stays paused: the probe can refute the concern only for the scenarios it drives, and it does not construct the configuration where the leader's latest snapshot index is below a follower's applied index, so no defect claim is made either way.\"}"}}
